  "narrative": {
    "intro": "W S Darley and obligated $933M in FY2026 to date across 1,755 awards. The average award size is $532K. Obligations are down 37.2% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $431M in FY21 to $1.5B in FY25, then moved to $933M in FY26. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $927M in FY2026 to date. Other federal buyers include the General Services Administration with $3.9M and the Department of Justice with $2M. Markets are concentrated: Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers accounts for $490M and All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing accounts for $406M. A range of smaller markets appears in FY2026 to date, including Photographic and Photocopying Equipment Manufacturing at $13.4M and Surgical Appliance and Supplies Manufacturing at $10.7M. The dataset notes that all figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, and that current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). This profile emphasizes defense-facing obligations and a narrow set of high-dollar NAICS categories.",
